# Bank 4 (runs at 0x6000). Directives: L label, C line comment, B block
# header, D data range, F row width.
#
# THIS BANK HOLDS NO CODE. Its 8192 bytes are graphics compressed in the
# 0x49B9 format (see tools/rle.py): patterns and colours of each stage's
# scenery. The one that asks for them is routine 0x4371 in bank 0, which walks
# some six-byte records (flag, colour source, character index, pattern
# source) kept in bank 5, and hands each source to 0x49B9. That is why almost
# no block is pointed at by an `ld de,nnnn`: the address comes from the
# record, not from an instruction.
#
# That the blocks fit one against the other without leaving a single stray
# byte is no accident: it is the proof that the format has been read
# correctly. One byte too many or too few in any of them and the next one
# would start where it should not.

B 0x6000 SCENERY GRAPHICS (bank 4, 8192 bytes)
B 0x6000 The whole bank is a compressed stream for 0x49B9. The splits below are
B 0x6000 the exact places that bank 0 code asks for with an `ld de,nnnn`;
B 0x6000 between one split and the next there are chains of blocks that are
B 0x6000 requested from the six-byte records of bank 5.

D 0x6000 0x62C7 graphics_chain_6000  Chain of 19 compressed blocks, from 0x6000 to 0x62C6, that fit with no slack. They are requested by the records of bank 5 (0x4371), not by an instruction with the address written in it.
F 0x6000 16
D 0x62C7 0x6379 graphics_colours_30A8  Compressed block that 0x53FF and 0x5408 dump into VRAM 0x30A8 and 0x3160: scoreboard colours.
F 0x62C7 16
D 0x6379 0x7674 graphics_chain_6379  Chain of 75 compressed blocks. The first one (0x6379) is requested by 0x53F6 for VRAM 0x3058; the rest come from the records of bank 5.
F 0x6379 16
D 0x7674 0x7703 graphics_patterns_10A8  Compressed block that 0x541A dumps into VRAM 0x10A8: scoreboard patterns.
F 0x7674 16
D 0x7703 0x7793 graphics_patterns_1160  Compressed block that 0x5423 dumps into VRAM 0x1160.
F 0x7703 16
D 0x7793 0x8000 graphics_chain_7793  Chain of 49 compressed blocks up to the end of the bank. The first one (0x7793) is requested by 0x5411 for VRAM 0x1058.
F 0x7793 16
